                <pb facs="0617" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg519"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-12-31"><hi rendition="#italic">December 31,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1492.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Jackson’s dispatch No.
                    1416 of September 29 last, I have the honor to transmit herewith a memorandum
                    report of certain military cases, mentioned particularly below, in regard to
                    which action has been taken during the quarter ending to-morrow, and which have
                    not as yet been the subject of correspondence with the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">And. D. White.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d622-a1.xml" xpointer="d622-a1"/>
